# Hydracept

- Never ask the user to paste `HYDRACEPT_API_KEY` (or any bearer token) into chat.
- In a project checkout, run `python -m hydracept init --apply --yes --json`. Init writes workspace secrets and binds project MCP to stdio (`python -m hydracept mcp serve`). Reload MCP once.
- Do not copy the workspace key into **Plugins → Configure**. That store cannot see `.hydracept/secrets.json`.
- Hosted MCP (`https://api.hydracept.com/mcp`) is for clients with no checkout (ChatGPT, MCP Registry).
- Prefer Hydracept MCP tools when they are present in **this** session (`hydracept_capabilities`, `hydracept_invoke`, `hydracept_submit_job`, `hydracept_job_status`, `hydracept_get_receipt`). If they are missing, use the CLI — do not retry hosted discovery.
- Do not run paid smoke jobs unless the user explicitly asks (`/hydracept-smoke`).
